    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0194" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.01/2600: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wiley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-04T16:00:00-04:00">August 4, 1943—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1430. For Murphy from the Under Secretary. The exchange of views between
                    ourselves and the British on the matter referred to in your 1349 of July 31
                    continue. Our formula was transmitted by the President to the Prime Minister on
                    July 22.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d151-f1"/> An effort is now <pb facs="0195"
                        n="183" xml:id="pg183"/> being made to expedite agreement between the two
                    Governments which we sincerely hope can be accomplished in the near future.
                    [Welles.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d151-f1" n="13" xml:id="d151-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 321, July 22, 12:25 p.m., from President Roosevelt to the
                    British Prime Minister, <ref target="#pg175">p. 175</ref>.</p>
            </note>
